[Music]  if you have some free time on your hands  and you don't know what to do with it we  have a cure for your boredom  these DIY crafts and projects will keep  you and your friends entertained for  hours if this is your first time  visiting our channel don't forget to  subscribe and please give this video a  big thumbs up  today we'll be sharing 10 pointless  projects guaranteed to waste your  precious time  chocolate playdough this no-bake  chocolate play-doh is not only fun but  it's edible too just mix together 2 cups  of flour 1/2 cup of table salt 1/2 cup  of cocoa one and a half cups of boiling  water three tablespoons of vegetable oil  and a half a teaspoon of vanilla in a  large bowl mix well until a ball starts  to form let the ball sit for a few  minutes and then knead it until it  becomes nice and soft the time will fly  by as you play and eat your new edible  project monster slime are you ready to  make some gooey slime that you can play  with all day long to make this sticky  monster slime just plays half a cup of  clear glue into a mixing bowl then add a  bit of food coloring  we like to color green because it  reminds us of big scary monsters then  add just a bit of liquid starch until  the mixture turns into slime now it's  ready to be stretched blocked and rolled  into a sticky ball for hours on end  phloem when you mix slime and foam  together it creates phloem it is a  string G and sticky paste that's so much  fun to play with to create this blob of  foam or 1/2 cup of glue into a bowl then  add your choice of food coloring and  stir next you're going to pour in 1/2  cup of liquid starch mix the ingredients  together well and squish the mixture  with your hands when the mixture becomes  a blob rinse it under running water for  a few seconds pour in some little  styrofoam balls and mix them into the  blob using your hands and there you have  it your phloem is complete marbles slime  this updated version of homemade slime  includes various colors to give it a  marbled effect all you have to do is mix  together 1/3 cup of warm water 1/2 cup  of glue and  add a bit of kool-aid or food coloring  of your choice stir it all together and  set it aside  then mix together a 3/4 cup of warm  water and 2 teaspoons of borax stir it  combine it with the first mixture and  work with your hands for 2 to 3 minutes  repeat these steps using different  colors of food coloring and then combine  the various colors have slimed together  to create marbled slime dough make quick  send get prepared to sink down deep into  your very own batch of homemade  quicksand to get started you'll need a  cup of corn starch 3/4 cups of water a  plastic bowl or bin and if you like you  can also use some food coloring make the  ingredients together for about 10  minutes until the consistency is just  right then go ahead and have some fun  sinking your hands and feet into this  fun DIY project suds eruption here's a  fun project you can do when you're  feeling a little bored it's called a  suds eruption all you need is a quarter  cup of clear hand soap 3/4 cups of warm  water 2 tablespoons of citric acid and  some food colorings mixing these  ingredients together will cause the suds  to become bigger and bigger until  they're overflowing all over the place  just make sure you have a set of towels  nearby for an easy cleanup  bubblegum the slime this slime looks  feels and smells just like real  bubblegum and we promise you won't be  able to stop playing with it as soon as  you get your hands on it just mix three  ounces of liquid starch with 8 ounces of  glue then add a bit of pink food  coloring to the mix and you have your  very own bubblegum slime place a straw  in the mixture and blow slowly to make  big and fun slime bubbles silky soft  goop this silky and smooth goop can be  made in any color your heart desires  just add a half a cup of cornstarch to  two ounces of liquid starch keep mixing  until it becomes smooth and soft and now  you're ready to enjoy running your  fingers through this super soft and  silky goop Orbeez slime how cool does  this look it's called Orbeez slime and  it's so addicting and fun to play with  just mix two bottles of glue and two  cups of water into a bowl then take a  separate Bowl and mix one teaspoon of  borax with one and a quarter cups of  water stir until the borax has dissolved  then slowly mix the borax water with the  glue mixture  add in as many Orbeez as you like and a  bit more for racks until your slime  feels just right we just love the way it  looks when it's all done we could stare  at it and play with it for hours  princess snot when a princess blows her  nose what color is our snot glittery  pink of course this is a fun project for  people of all ages just take a half cup  of hot water and add two and a half  tablespoons of unflavored gelatin and a  quarter cup of corn syrup but don't  forget to have the pink food coloring  then add glitter flakes to the mixture  and you're all done which of these  pointless projects will you be trying in  your free time let us know in the  comment section down below and don't  forget to give this video a big thumbs  up  [Music]

